  "wikidataId": "Q10825609",
  "geometryBasis": "The native named fort outline and moat geometry establish the bastioned site. Seven mapped wall fragments, four bridge crossings, stairs, exhibition hall and both tiers of the central mound set the present layout.",
  "sectionBasis": "The Department of Cultural Heritage identifies the surviving north arcade and roofed south entrance, historic losses, restored crossings, 1997 memorial mound and 8.1 m lamp. Prof MK’s two public-domain photographs show the stone south gate and the black student memorial.",
  "limitations": [
    "The model represents the memorial site and surviving masonry. The vanished northwestern works and former grand gate towers at the east and west entries are outside the standing reconstruction.",
    "The gate photo shows the site in 2012. Its event banner, flags and other temporary objects have been omitted from the structure.",
    "Wall fragment heights, parapet details, the central lamp’s section, the small exhibition building’s elevations and the student memorial’s position inside the documented northeastern quadrant are estimated."
